      },
      {
       "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
       "source": "PubMed",
       "id": "29287774"
      }
     ],
     "value": "Involved in peroxisomal beta-oxidation of branched-chain fatty acids (BCFAs). Catalyzes the initial and rate-limiting dehydrogenation step that removes two hydrogen molecules and introduces a trans double bond between the alpha and beta carbons of the acyl CoA molecules while generating hydrogen peroxide as a by-product (PubMed:29287774). Metabolizes multi-methyl-branched fatty acyl-CoA esters such as (2S)-pristanoyl-CoA, displaying redundancy with ACOX3 (PubMed:29287774). Can oxidize straight-chain mono- and dicarboxylyl fatty acyl-CoAs with lower efficiency (By similarity) (PubMed:29287774)"
    }
   ],
